(window.XP_SOLUTIONS=window.XP_SOLUTIONS||{})["s08"]={"$schema":"../../schema/scenario-solution.schema.json","summary":"Yes, Sarah can present. The last successful refresh (Sunday 06:05) already contains the closed May ledger, because postings stopped on Friday at 18:00. The failure only means Monday's data is missing, and the board pack doesn't show June. Two weekend changes caused the failure: the DW team renamed vw_Customer.CustomerSegment to Segment (CHG-4471, 02:00 Monday), and IT rotated service-account passwords (CHG-4472, Sunday 22:00), which invalidated the treasury connection. Fix the credential and the column reference, refresh after the meeting, then fix the process: alerts to a team, schema changes announced to BI, and credentials owned by the source team.","root_cause":["DimCustomer: refresh_error.json says column CustomerSegment wasn't found; vw_customer_columns.csv shows it renamed to Segment at 02:10 by CHG-4471 (\"rename columns to the new naming standard\"). BI wasn't notified.","FxRates: invalid credentials for sql-treasury as svc_treasury_read; last successful auth Sunday 05:44; CHG-4472 rotated svc_* passwords on Sunday at 22:00, after Sunday's refresh had already run.","Detection: the failure email went only to the listed owner, Sam, who is on holiday. The incident was noticed 45 minutes later because Nina saw the timestamp.","Contributing: the model has no tolerance for a renamed column, and nobody owns the treasury credential on the BI side."],"steps":["07:05 Acknowledge to Nina: \"Looking at it now, update by 07:30.\" Start a timeline.","07:10 Impact first: refresh_history.csv shows Sunday 06:05 Completed; the close calendar says May postings ended Friday 18:00. So Sunday's data has every May posting. The pack is complete for the board.","07:15 Gateway healthy (gateway_status.csv), so not an infrastructure outage. refresh_error.json shows two distinct errors on two sources.","07:20 Match each error to a change: CHG-4471 (renamed CustomerSegment) and CHG-4472 (rotated svc passwords).","07:30 Reply to Sarah: \"You can present from the dashboard. It shows data as of Sun 7 Jun 06:05, which includes the full May close. Today's refresh failed for reasons unrelated to May's numbers; we're fixing it and will not touch the model before 09:30.\"","07:35 Mitigate safely, not during the meeting: get the new svc_treasury_read password from finance.systems (the owner) and update the gateway connection; agree with Kenji to add CustomerSegment back as an alias column in vw_Customer temporarily (no model change needed before the meeting).","09:35 After the board meeting: refresh on demand, verify row counts and the May totals unchanged, then update everyone.","Permanent fix: change the Power Query step to use Segment (and remove the alias in a planned change), store the treasury credential under a service owner with rotation notified to BI, route failure notifications to a team mailbox or on-call, and add the BI team to the DW change approval list.","Write the postmortem within 48 hours: blameless, with actions, owners and dates."],"numbers":{"title":"Timeline (Monday 8 June unless stated)","cols":["Time","Event"],"rows":[["Sun 06:05","Last successful refresh; includes all May postings (ledger locked Fri 18:00)"],["Sun 22:00","CHG-4472 rotates svc_* service account passwords"],["02:00–02:10","CHG-4471 renames vw_Customer.CustomerSegment → Segment"],["05:30","Scheduled refresh starts"],["06:17","Refresh fails (2 errors); email to the owner, who is on holiday"],["07:02","Nina notices the timestamp and reports it (detection +45 min)"],["07:30","CFO told she can present from Sunday's data"],["07:40","Gateway credential updated; temporary alias column added to the view by DW team"],["08:30","Board meeting proceeds with closed May figures"],["09:35–10:12","On-demand refresh succeeds; totals verified unchanged"]]},"artifacts":[{"title":"Postmortem actions","lang":"md","body":["| Action | Owner | Due |","|---|---|---|","| Refresh failure alerts go to bi-oncall@ (not one person) for all certified models | Elena | 12 Jun |","| BI team added as approver on DW changes that touch views used by certified models | Kenji | 19 Jun |","| View contract: columns used by BI documented; renames get a deprecation period with alias | Kenji | 30 Jun |","| Credential rotation for svc_* accounts used by gateways notifies the connection owners | IT identity | 30 Jun |","| Power Query step updated to Segment; alias removed in a planned change | You | 16 Jun |","| Runbook: \"refresh failed\" triage starts with impact (what data is affected) before fixing | You | 12 Jun |"]},{"title":"07:30 message to the CFO","lang":"md","body":["Sarah, you can present from the dashboard. It shows data as of Sunday 7 June 06:05, which includes every May posting (the ledger closed on Friday at 18:00). This morning's refresh failed because of two IT changes over the weekend; it doesn't affect May's numbers. We won't change anything until after your meeting, and I'll confirm when the refresh is fixed."]}],"communication":{"executive":"The board pack numbers are correct and complete for May. This morning's automatic update failed because of two IT changes over the weekend, which affected only today's update. It's fixed, and we've changed how such changes are announced and how failures are reported.","engineer":"Two errors in one refresh: Expression.Error on DimCustomer (CustomerSegment renamed to Segment by CHG-4471) and invalid credentials on the Treasury source (svc password rotated by CHG-4472 after Sunday's run). Mitigated with credential update plus temporary alias in vw_Customer; permanent: PQ uses Segment, view contract, rotation notifications, alerts to bi-oncall@."},"pitfalls":["Fixing first, assessing impact second. At 07:05 the most valuable fact is that Sunday's data already contains the closed month.","Editing Power Query in production at 08:15 to rename the column, starting a 35-minute refresh during the meeting.","Finding the column rename and stopping. The credential failure would have failed the next refresh too.","A postmortem that says \"Kenji's team broke the view\". Blameless means fixing the process that let it happen."],"review":{"junior":"Starts editing the model immediately, triggers refreshes before 08:30, and tells the CFO \"it's broken\" without saying whether her numbers are affected.","competent":"Finds the renamed column, fixes it and refreshes before the meeting.","senior":"Separates impact from cause, tells the CFO by 07:30 she can present with evidence, finds both causes from the change calendar, mitigates without risk, refreshes after the meeting and writes a blameless postmortem with owners.","architect":"Treats it as a contract problem between data platform and BI: data contracts for views used by certified models, change approval, service-owned credentials, team alerting and refresh-failure SLOs."}};
